WEBVTT

00:19.280 --> 00:21.170
<i>and wandered into the asteroid field.</i>

00:21.630 --> 00:21.780
150ms lag

00:23.700 --> 00:25.370
Back off!

00:28.610 --> 00:31.590
I'll kill 'em if you come any closer!

00:28.960 --> 00:32.100
<i>Myce Authorities have begun rescue efforts,</i>

00:32.100 --> 00:35.470
<i>but it will take time due to the dangerous environment.</i>

00:35.470 --> 00:37.950
<i>The distress signal was sent by Mr. Puttabaya,</i>

00:37.950 --> 00:41.270
<i>who is also a passenger inside the ship.</i>

00:42.350 --> 00:43.560
What the...

00:46.110 --> 00:47.640
Nanpaa, you fugitive!

00:47.640 --> 00:48.980
You're mine now!

00:49.240 --> 00:50.740
Oh, really?

00:59.240 --> 01:01.080
That's for not cooperating.

01:11.130 --> 01:11.920
Fujikuro!

01:13.120 --> 01:14.380
Move, Iria!

01:14.700 --> 01:16.310
Stay out of this!

01:19.790 --> 01:22.140
I'll take this bastard!

01:22.360 --> 01:24.320
You goddamned thief!

01:25.030 --> 01:27.070
That's harsh.

01:27.070 --> 01:30.050
Besides, you're still an apprentice, so I'll take the credit for this one!

01:30.050 --> 01:30.940
What?

01:33.070 --> 01:36.570
Stop wearing men's hair beads and try using make-up like a girl.

01:37.940 --> 01:39.660
Say hi to your brother for me!

01:40.010 --> 01:41.940
You slimebag!

01:45.790 --> 01:47.450
I'm so sorry!

01:48.810 --> 01:49.880
Thank you!

01:51.150 --> 01:52.640
Thanks!

01:53.260 --> 01:55.090
Hurry, I gotta go, too!

02:19.280 --> 02:26.750
<i>The night sky has betrayed the stars...</i>

02:29.800 --> 02:37.400
<i>A faraway cry slowly fades.</i>

02:40.270 --> 02:50.980
<i>The sun has disappeared...</i>

02:50.980 --> 03:01.330
<i>and my heart is alone with the revelation.</i>

03:03.870 --> 03:12.880
<i>A stranger's dreams appear.</i>

03:14.340 --> 03:22.710
<i>Tempting lost souls.</i>

03:24.770 --> 03:32.820
<i>A stranger's dreams appear.</i>

03:30.770 --> 03:34.670
Iria: Zeiram the Animation

03:34.670 --> 03:37.820
Pitch Black

03:44.170 --> 03:46.280
That was not funny!

03:46.650 --> 03:50.580
Give him a cut of the action once in a while. It's professional courtesy.

03:50.810 --> 03:52.820
No, that was stealing, pure and simple.

03:52.820 --> 03:54.530
Don't be so harsh.

03:54.530 --> 03:56.900
I should have gone with you.

03:56.900 --> 03:58.920
I could've handled it by myself.

04:01.590 --> 04:02.850
I'm leaving with Bob.

04:02.850 --> 04:04.630
We have a long flight ahead.

04:04.630 --> 04:05.800
Take care of the house.

04:07.330 --> 04:08.310
Bob!

04:08.540 --> 04:10.520
Long time no see!

04:11.500 --> 04:14.020
Big Brother, you always get all the fun jobs!

04:14.020 --> 04:16.490
I don't know if this will be "fun", exactly.

04:17.500 --> 04:18.730
Be careful, okay?

04:19.370 --> 04:20.800
For good luck.

04:29.650 --> 04:32.610
— What is that?
— A micro comm.

04:32.610 --> 04:34.620
A present from Iria?

04:36.660 --> 04:38.370
She's got you on a tight leash.

04:39.560 --> 04:40.900
Fujikuro!

04:40.900 --> 04:44.570
Bob, you gotta send some decent jobs my way, too.

04:44.570 --> 04:46.510
Don't you think you're giving too much to Glen?

04:46.900 --> 04:48.860
The results speak for themselves.

04:48.860 --> 04:51.570
I match the right talent to the job.

04:51.570 --> 04:54.600
Fujikuro, you pulled a dirty move on my sister.

04:54.730 --> 04:58.560
You let an apprentice go out alone, that's against the rules!

04:59.280 --> 05:01.280
Glen, we don't have time.

05:02.350 --> 05:05.050
It looks like this job is worth a lot of cash.

05:05.050 --> 05:07.440
Give me a 40% cut, and I'll help you out.

05:07.440 --> 05:09.280
Fujikuro! Over here!

05:10.190 --> 05:11.080
Iria!

05:11.210 --> 05:14.080
Squeeze that trigger, and we're all toast!

05:16.060 --> 05:16.910
Dammit!

05:16.910 --> 05:18.110
Not if you know how to use it.

05:18.110 --> 05:20.540
Besides, you owe me. Hurry up!

05:22.040 --> 05:27.830
Iria, thanks for the help, but use a different method next time.

05:32.190 --> 05:33.200
Oh well...

05:33.200 --> 05:34.640
Hold it!

05:34.850 --> 05:37.100
Did I give you permission to move?

05:43.930 --> 05:45.740
Who are these guys?

05:45.740 --> 05:48.080
<i>This is a message for Bob of Ghomvak Security.</i>

05:48.080 --> 05:51.910
<i>Tedan Tippedai has cancelled your current assignment.</i>

05:52.580 --> 05:53.790
What's going on here?

05:52.580 --> 05:54.820
<i>The assignment has been cancelled.</i>

05:53.790 --> 05:54.830
Keep moving!

05:54.830 --> 05:57.070
<i>Cancellation fees will be paid in full.</i>

05:54.830 --> 05:57.070
We don't have time for this crap.

05:57.070 --> 05:58.670
I'll explain later.

06:01.320 --> 06:02.670
Let's go!

06:10.470 --> 06:12.770
That's one messed up welcome party!

06:12.770 --> 06:13.870
Later, Fujikuro.

06:13.870 --> 06:15.350
Not so fast!

06:15.780 --> 06:17.080
Don't use that weapon!

06:17.080 --> 06:18.720
It's not safe, even if you know how to use it!

06:46.300 --> 06:47.390
Damn!

06:47.390 --> 06:49.260
That's a cheap trick!

06:52.460 --> 06:54.680
Wasting my time!

07:02.440 --> 07:02.980
Fujikuro!

07:06.010 --> 07:06.970
What the...

07:11.950 --> 07:17.300
This assignment caused a serious split within Tedan Tippedai itself.

07:17.300 --> 07:20.580
A bad one. It's probably an issue with the cargo.

07:22.620 --> 07:25.270
It looks like it's gonna be a screwed up assignment.

07:25.270 --> 07:27.630
Are you sure we're gonna get paid?

07:28.960 --> 07:31.680
When did money become an issue for you?

07:32.270 --> 07:34.920
I'm not looking to waste my time.

07:34.920 --> 07:36.970
Saving lives is a waste of time?

07:48.150 --> 07:49.940
Stop that!

07:51.290 --> 07:52.490
What are you doing?

07:52.920 --> 07:54.450
Where are we going?

07:56.620 --> 07:57.590
Fujikuro!

07:57.590 --> 08:00.630
It's a shortcut. I know where they're headed.

08:00.630 --> 08:02.750
You're gonna just leave them while they're under attack?

08:02.770 --> 08:05.420
Damn right! It's none of my business.

08:05.420 --> 08:07.710
Do you think those two can't handle a few machines?

08:15.510 --> 08:17.010
Iria's following us?

08:17.010 --> 08:19.580
She probably heard the gunshots.

08:19.580 --> 08:22.470
She worships you. What did you expect?

08:26.990 --> 08:30.560
I always told her, "make a decision and follow through."

08:30.560 --> 08:33.790
So, did you let Iria go out on a job by herself again?

08:33.790 --> 08:34.460
Yeah.

08:34.460 --> 08:36.170
I already told you to stop.

08:36.170 --> 08:39.870
She still doesn't have her full licence, it's against regulations.

08:40.230 --> 08:42.490
She can handle it.

08:42.490 --> 08:44.280
She's not old enough.

08:44.280 --> 08:46.590
She will be on her next birthday.

08:47.470 --> 08:49.710
— On her birthday?
— Yeah.

08:51.380 --> 08:56.300
She's exactly like you. I can't imagine why.

09:15.770 --> 09:17.670
Still hanging on?

09:18.770 --> 09:20.490
There's the teleport gate.

09:20.870 --> 09:22.960
They're planning to leave from there.

09:22.960 --> 09:24.460
You're right, for a change.

09:32.420 --> 09:33.460
That little...

09:43.460 --> 09:44.870
Stay out of it!

09:44.870 --> 09:46.260
Do you wanna die?

09:46.650 --> 09:48.480
Why do you think I followed them?

09:48.940 --> 09:50.380
We don't have time to help them!

09:50.380 --> 09:53.010
She's come this far. What's the big deal?

09:53.010 --> 09:55.150
We've gotta catch our transit!

09:55.150 --> 09:57.070
It's not like we can cancel it!

09:58.810 --> 10:01.120
We'll ride out on their teleport link!

10:01.330 --> 10:02.830
I won't let you interfere with their job!

10:03.080 --> 10:06.210
Even if we miss our transit, we still have to pay!

10:06.210 --> 10:09.560
Do you always have to be so prepared?

10:09.560 --> 10:10.500
Gate eight.

10:12.670 --> 10:13.380
Iria!

10:15.560 --> 10:18.820
Glen, I'm against taking Iria with us.

10:18.820 --> 10:21.050
Do you want me to abandon her?

10:21.050 --> 10:22.810
Iria can take care of herself.

10:28.240 --> 10:30.360
Iria, just get off!

10:30.360 --> 10:33.110
We might get shot off into space!

10:33.260 --> 10:35.850
Get off? You mean fall off!

10:35.850 --> 10:36.820
Fujikuro, another one!

10:38.550 --> 10:40.240
Are they insane?

10:43.660 --> 10:46.200
They're gonna get all of you for destruction of public property.

10:55.180 --> 10:56.840
Bastards!

11:03.240 --> 11:03.930
Iria!

11:05.080 --> 11:05.860
Glen!

11:05.860 --> 11:07.640
You won't make it, you'll get shot!

11:14.110 --> 11:16.320
Damn, you're both so reckless!

11:23.930 --> 11:24.530
It's time!

11:35.680 --> 11:37.340
I missed it!

12:04.100 --> 12:07.680
— What's the assignment?
— The Karma. It looks like a hijacking.

12:07.680 --> 12:10.580
I heard about it on TV. So, it's not an accident.

12:10.580 --> 12:13.770
Our job is to evacuate all passengers, crew and cargo.

12:13.770 --> 12:17.670
Everything has to be finished before the authorities arrive.

12:18.920 --> 12:20.170
I see...

12:37.670 --> 12:39.290
We only have one chance.

12:39.290 --> 12:42.570
We won't have time to think once we've been detected.

12:43.110 --> 12:44.450
We're on our way right now?

12:44.450 --> 12:48.080
Right. We're going to make direct contact with the Karma's computer.

12:48.780 --> 12:51.700
If we're lucky, the hijackers won't even know we're there.

12:51.700 --> 12:54.710
If they detect us, we'll have to act quickly, right?

12:54.710 --> 12:55.540
I see it!

12:58.930 --> 13:00.220
It's all right.

13:00.220 --> 13:03.260
I'm very friendly with the Karma's computer.

13:18.460 --> 13:19.060
Bob?

13:20.680 --> 13:23.400
Apparently, the enemy got a grip on your friend.

13:25.690 --> 13:28.720
Karma's a mid-sized transport vessel, meaning that the cargo bays can be...

13:28.720 --> 13:29.950
...accessed from the outside.

13:31.760 --> 13:32.700
Let's move!

13:36.000 --> 13:37.550
The ship has three escape pods.

13:37.550 --> 13:41.100
Two above the rear hangar and one under the bridge.

13:41.100 --> 13:42.910
Each pod holds six people.

13:42.910 --> 13:46.040
It should be on manual control if the computer was having issues...

13:46.040 --> 13:47.720
What if we can't use the escape pods?

13:47.990 --> 13:48.940
We'll use these.

13:48.940 --> 13:50.480
We can tow them with the Kreper.

13:50.480 --> 13:53.870
It won't be fun, but it beats dying.

13:59.090 --> 14:01.540
This hijacker's insane!

14:01.540 --> 14:03.230
He destroyed the computer!

14:12.870 --> 14:15.830
Looks like the computer's on-line after all.

14:43.930 --> 14:45.720
I'll check out the residential block.

14:46.030 --> 14:48.530
Fine, Iria, cover me!

14:59.610 --> 15:02.440
Bob, what's going on? The cargo's missing!

15:02.440 --> 15:03.420
<i>What?</i>

15:03.420 --> 15:04.840
The hangar's empty.

15:05.990 --> 15:08.790
Both escape pods look functional.

15:22.740 --> 15:24.480
Shit!

15:29.410 --> 15:31.190
It's a bloody mess down here.

15:31.190 --> 15:33.160
This isn't your average hijacker, for sure.

15:33.430 --> 15:35.620
Yeah, looks that way.

15:45.160 --> 15:48.600
<i>Found ’em. Looks like the surviving crew members are all together.</i>

15:48.600 --> 15:51.800
You found survivors? I see bodies everywhere.

15:52.470 --> 15:53.830
Watch your back.

15:53.830 --> 15:57.760
The crew can't tell me any info on the hijackers.
They're really scared.

15:58.300 --> 16:01.520
<i>No sign of the Vice President, he could be dead or alive.</i>

16:01.520 --> 16:02.730
Got it.

16:03.380 --> 16:07.300
Where's the cargo? The hangar's clean.
My partner confirmed it.

16:07.300 --> 16:09.050
— Did it move?
— Yes.

16:09.050 --> 16:10.920
— Where?
— I don't know.

16:10.920 --> 16:12.990
Who moved it?

16:14.150 --> 16:15.200
It moved by itself.

16:15.420 --> 16:16.480
What?

16:16.480 --> 16:18.550
The VP went to look for it.

16:18.550 --> 16:21.160
Huh? Either way, we've got to get you out.

16:21.760 --> 16:23.620
We can leave?

16:23.930 --> 16:26.590
Of course. Let's move!

16:29.540 --> 16:31.460
— Let's check the engine room.
— Okay.

16:35.390 --> 16:37.300
W-Wait! Don't shoot!

16:38.470 --> 16:39.430
You're Puttabaya!

16:39.710 --> 16:41.890
That's right, can I put my arms down?

16:42.520 --> 16:44.770
I'm Glen, a Hunter. I'm here to rescue you.

16:45.210 --> 16:47.950
I sent the SOS signal.

16:47.950 --> 16:51.340
Tell me what happened, something went seriously wrong inside this ship.

16:58.500 --> 16:59.530
That's...

17:12.550 --> 17:14.380
— Watch out, Iria!
— No!

17:17.320 --> 17:19.010
Don't shoot him!

17:28.930 --> 17:29.520
Iria!

17:39.000 --> 17:41.490
I've heard rumours about you.

17:41.490 --> 17:43.910
Iria, take him and find Bob.

17:44.160 --> 17:45.860
What are you going to do with him?

17:45.860 --> 17:47.330
— Let's go!
— Hurry!

17:52.990 --> 17:54.940
Let my brother handle it! Hurry!

17:54.940 --> 17:56.720
— But, he's...
— Let's go!

18:02.800 --> 18:05.680
Bob, our hijacker is that immortal, hat-wearing creature!

18:05.680 --> 18:06.350
<i>What?</i>

18:06.790 --> 18:10.160
I'm sure of it. He's a monster, just like the rumours say.

18:13.550 --> 18:16.360
You don't feel a thing, either, huh?

18:26.490 --> 18:28.960
You're the first bastard to ever throw me.

18:46.740 --> 18:49.690
Just get to the TransSat, and you'll be all right.

18:50.000 --> 18:52.450
— Thank you.
— It's my job.

18:57.520 --> 18:59.320
Vice President!

18:59.990 --> 19:01.530
Don't step on those things on the floor.

19:05.460 --> 19:06.910
What are you doing?

19:06.910 --> 19:10.620
So, it looks like Tedan Tippedai didn't cancel the Zeiram project?

19:11.260 --> 19:12.210
Zeiram?

19:12.420 --> 19:15.930
In that case, consider your contract with Ghomvak Security null and void!

19:15.930 --> 19:19.590
What are you talking about? There have been no violations!

20:09.820 --> 20:11.140
Stay right there...

20:30.360 --> 20:31.960
We have to bring Zeiram back with us!

20:32.250 --> 20:33.500
You're crazy!

20:33.500 --> 20:35.970
You want to bring an indestructible murderer back?

20:35.970 --> 20:40.150
Dr. Touka's Report classifies that freak as a Class A threat!

20:40.150 --> 20:42.420
Your crew paid for that monster with their lives!

20:42.640 --> 20:45.660
Recovering the cargo is part of the contract!

20:45.660 --> 20:47.400
Glen!

20:47.400 --> 20:48.850
Answer me!

20:50.000 --> 20:50.810
Wait, Iria!

20:51.730 --> 20:53.220
Let me tell you something.

20:53.220 --> 20:55.950
There was an attempt to prevent us from doing this job.

20:55.950 --> 20:56.730
What?

20:56.730 --> 21:00.740
That means there's a faction that opposes the Zeiram project.

21:00.740 --> 21:03.930
They want the monster destroyed, along with this ship and its crew.

21:03.930 --> 21:07.660
Spineless cowards! They're all clueless idiots!

21:07.920 --> 21:10.580
As long as you're the only casualty, I'll cast my vote with them.

21:10.970 --> 21:12.920
You'll pay for that later!

21:12.920 --> 21:16.060
I'll make sure they're aware that you're responsible for the victims here.

21:16.060 --> 21:16.960
Bob!

21:23.730 --> 21:25.120
Get in!

21:27.420 --> 21:28.640
Iria, get inside the pod!

21:32.340 --> 21:34.060
Just freeze him!

21:34.300 --> 21:38.270
Yeah, but if he melts out, he'll start killing again! Let's go!

21:40.550 --> 21:41.610
Stop!

21:47.220 --> 21:50.620
T-This is very important to me.

21:51.160 --> 21:52.700
Bob!

21:53.080 --> 21:54.520
Bob!

21:55.290 --> 21:57.670
Leave, Iria!

21:58.350 --> 22:00.130
Bob, let him go!

22:00.360 --> 22:02.240
That's not gonna kill him.

22:02.240 --> 22:04.090
Leave while you still have the chance!

22:04.370 --> 22:05.870
Bob!

22:05.870 --> 22:09.550
Hurry! I can't hold him back!

22:12.010 --> 22:12.970
Bob!

22:14.770 --> 22:18.480
This is our chance! Freeze it while it's distracted!

22:20.060 --> 22:22.370
You want me to freeze Bob along with the monster?

22:22.370 --> 22:24.280
What are you doing?

22:24.280 --> 22:27.930
Making sure that you get back to Myce alive.

22:27.930 --> 22:29.910
That's my minimum duty as a Hunter!

22:30.210 --> 22:33.910
You won't get your money without the cargo!

22:33.910 --> 22:37.160
Would you even sacrifice the girl in your picture to recover the cargo?

22:37.600 --> 22:39.120
What?

22:48.720 --> 22:51.090
— What are you doing?
— Try not to talk.

23:03.530 --> 23:05.030
Move!

23:07.730 --> 23:11.160
I'll kick your butt if Bob doesn't make it!

23:12.700 --> 23:17.620
You're just like Glen, I can't imagine why...

23:18.000 --> 23:19.410
Because he's my brother.

23:28.620 --> 23:31.880
— We don't have time for good-byes.
— I know.

23:46.200 --> 23:47.310
What is it?

23:47.310 --> 23:48.770
Something important.

23:53.450 --> 23:55.690
— How's your leg?
— It's fine.

23:55.690 --> 23:56.870
So you can't kill him?

23:57.300 --> 23:58.630
According to the rumours...

23:58.630 --> 24:01.520
That can't be true, though.

24:01.520 --> 24:04.720
He seems to be controlling the ship.

24:04.720 --> 24:07.910
I can't believe they brought that thing on board.

24:07.910 --> 24:11.260
— Do you have any ideas?
— Blow the ship.

24:11.600 --> 24:14.770
A bit extreme, but better than ignoring that monster.

24:14.770 --> 24:16.140
Let's go!

24:31.950 --> 24:32.780
Glen, look!

24:41.730 --> 24:43.710
It's smarter than it looks...

24:47.130 --> 24:49.670
Iria, get in! Throw me a Plunchit!

24:55.940 --> 24:56.800
Thanks!

25:03.780 --> 25:05.310
Plunchit...

25:12.860 --> 25:13.990
Iria, activate your shield!

25:29.060 --> 25:29.920
Hurry!

25:30.440 --> 25:32.860
Leave! I'll use the pod under the bridge!

25:32.860 --> 25:33.970
Raise your shield!

25:36.880 --> 25:37.930
Glen!

25:39.220 --> 25:41.120
Get as far away as you can.

25:41.120 --> 25:42.890
Take care of yourself, all right?

25:56.330 --> 25:57.700
Glen!

26:15.130 --> 26:18.810
They brought a real nightmare on board this vessel...

27:00.470 --> 27:05.720
<i>The morning to come does not matter,</i>

27:05.720 --> 27:13.210
<i>let's go as we are now.</i>

27:19.120 --> 27:25.270
<i>We're passing a blue star,</i>

27:25.270 --> 27:31.610
<i>a tiny floating light.</i>

27:31.610 --> 27:37.920
<i>It's just the two of us, no need to speak.</i>

27:37.920 --> 27:43.670
<i>Looking out over the city...</i>

27:43.670 --> 27:49.890
<i>The painful memories we have shared,</i>

27:49.890 --> 27:55.190
<i>they will be put to rest tonight.</i>

27:55.190 --> 28:01.740
<i>And the night to come does not matter,</i>

28:01.740 --> 28:08.980
<i>let's go without looking back.</i>

28:08.980 --> 28:14.180
<i>Even though our dreams are far away,</i>

28:14.180 --> 28:21.610
<i>I will never let them go.</i>

28:34.730 --> 28:38.440
Taowajan, a planet located at the frontier of the Myce system.

28:38.960 --> 28:42.990
Iria makes an emergency landing on this peaceful resort planet.

28:43.990 --> 28:45.530
What will await Iria there?

28:46.410 --> 28:48.160
Dirty angels...

28:48.670 --> 28:51.080
Cold-hearted caretakers of Utopia...

28:51.270 --> 28:52.160
The man who brings death...

28:52.330 --> 28:55.420
Now, you'll have to deal with me!

28:55.420 --> 28:59.130
Rampage.
